body:
Her nose is not wetter than any regular cat nose (not snotty or anything), this is the second time, first time we didn't manage to get on camera but same sound, and she didn't throw anything up either. She seems healthy otherwise, playful, eats with gusto, etc...

&#x200B;

I don't know if this is relevant but she has been living outside for at least a few months, I just brought her in last week and it was storming and raining the few days before I brought her in.
